<title>CANADA: Cam-Net fires chairman.</title>
<headline>Cam-Net fires chairman.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cam-Net Communications Network Inc said on Tuesday it fired its chairman, Daryl Buerge.</p>
<p>The board said it appointed an interim management group with board oversight to run day to day operations. The board said it ordered an independent audit to review all financial reporting by the company.</p>
<p>The board said the investigation to date had not revealed any company involvement in the transactions underlying the allegations against Buerge. The Federal Bureau of Investigation has laid charges of conspiring to commit securities fraud against Buerge.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto bureau 416-941-8100</p>
</text>
